{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20051",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 3.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Good afternoon, how are you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.19,
      "end_seconds": 7.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Start wherever you like, I'm listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.67,
      "end_seconds": 10.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "It's numbness in my fingers, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.88,
      "end_seconds": 15.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "So, how long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.26,
      "end_seconds": 19.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "About... well, about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.6,
      "end_seconds": 30.8,
      "duration_seconds": 10.2,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.82,
      "end_seconds": 49.72,
      "duration_seconds": 16.9,
      "text": "I'd say severe. It's worse with night. I get some relief from shaking my hand. Actually, I've had tingling in my thumb and first two fingers too, for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.52,
      "end_seconds": 55.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.35,
      "end_seconds": 72.98,
      "duration_seconds": 15.63,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, a six out of ten, I suppose. I'd say every other day. Right, I had dropping things before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.04,
      "end_seconds": 81.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any weight loss, fever or injury to the wrist?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.29,
      "end_seconds": 86.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Let me think, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.67,
      "end_seconds": 92.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Has there been any swelling of the wrist?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.08,
      "end_seconds": 96.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "No, no swelling of the wrist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.63,
      "end_seconds": 101.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Okay, is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.39,
      "end_seconds": 110.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Erm, no, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.94,
      "end_seconds": 114.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.49,
      "end_seconds": 119.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.14,
      "end_seconds": 136.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.97,
      "end_seconds": 142.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Mm, just a triple bypass, eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.46,
      "end_seconds": 147.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.72,
      "end_seconds": 157.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "Erm, I've had diabetes, yes. I've had an underactive thyroid for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.41,
      "end_seconds": 164.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "I see, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.16,
      "end_seconds": 170.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Let me think, I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.91,
      "end_seconds": 174.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.29,
      "end_seconds": 194.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.43,
      "end_seconds": 205.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "I'm on clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day. Before this I was on metformin; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.47,
      "end_seconds": 225.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.21,
      "end_seconds": 231.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "I have about eight cigarettes in a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.98,
      "end_seconds": 234.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.04,
      "end_seconds": 240.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.55,
      "end_seconds": 245.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.67,
      "end_seconds": 249.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.07,
      "end_seconds": 253.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Alright, is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.18,
      "end_seconds": 258.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.65,
      "end_seconds": 264.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.31,
      "end_seconds": 269.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.49,
      "end_seconds": 275.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Okay, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.25,
      "end_seconds": 279.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 280.06,
      "end_seconds": 291.41,
      "duration_seconds": 11.35,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Saturation 97 percent, respiratory rate 18, blood pressure 116 over 79. Temperature 36.7, pulse is 79 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.77,
      "end_seconds": 294.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.3,
      "end_seconds": 298.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.99,
      "end_seconds": 302.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.85,
      "end_seconds": 322.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.02,
      "text": "Tapping over the wrist brings on the tingling, and the muscle at the base of the thumb looks slightly thin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.18,
      "end_seconds": 332.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "You can relax now. Taking everything into account, it points towards carpal tunnel syndrome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.67,
      "end_seconds": 337.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.95,
      "end_seconds": 361.03,
      "duration_seconds": 21.08,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now carpal tunnel syndrome is my leading thought, not anything worse. We should do blood tests for numbness. A wrist splint at night will often settle it. Occupational therapy would be the right next step, I'll refer you. Let's review you in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.89,
      "end_seconds": 365.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.02,
      "end_seconds": 371.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.89,
      "end_seconds": 376.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}